{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And now let Pharaoh see.</b> Since El, blessed be He, made known the coming famine in order that you might seek to save your people, and showed you the plenty in order to inform you by what means you shall save them, it is fitting for you — so that you not sin against Him — to take action." "<b>A man discerning and wise.</b> Both contemplative and practical in the governance of states — עיוני ומעשי — so that he devote his attention to this matter; and the king need not be troubled [with it himself]."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "The verb תראה at the end is rendered 'take action,' reading it as 'you should see [to it]' in light of Joseph's directive to Pharaoh. The syntax of the final clause is compressed.", 1 "The Aramaic phrase מלכא לא להוי נזיק ('the king should not be harmed/troubled') echoes rabbinic idiom (Shabbat 150a); rendered here as 'need not be troubled.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:12.007797132Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}